---
description: Anonymous git identity and no secrets in git
alwaysApply: true
---

Never run git commit, merge, rebase, cherry-pick, pull-with-merge, annotated tag, or notes with a private inbox. Always set `GIT_AUTHOR_*` and `GIT_COMMITTER_*` to `Cursor Agent <cursoragent@noreply.github.com>` or use `git -c user.email=cursoragent@noreply.github.com`. A `*@users.noreply.github.com` address is also allowed. Never run `git config` to change identity.

Never stage, commit, or push secrets, credentials, passwords, tokens, private keys, `.env*` (except `.env.example`), `.netrc`, `.npmrc`, `.pypirc`, or credential JSON. Do not use `--no-verify`. If a hook denies the action, stop. Follow `/skills/git-safety/SKILL.md`.
